# 004_sv_polarization — outgroup polarization of SyRI SVs (inventory B1 #7)

Decides, for each SV in the 30 pairs of `../002_alignment`, which of the two genomes
carries the change (insertion vs deletion on which lineage), using genomes outside the
pair as outgroups. Fixes the reference-dependent ins/del asymmetry.

## Design
- Focal pairs: the 30 within-set pairs of 002 (diploid x diploid, diploid x Cbp subgenome,
  Cbp x Cbp). Events: syri INS/DEL >= 50 bp; INV/TRANS/INVTR >= 50 bp. DUP/INVDP are
  counted but not polarized.
- Outgroups: diploid x diploid and diploid x Cbp use the diploids of the *other* set
  (Cr/Cg for Co pairs, Co for Cr pairs); Cbp x Cbp uses the within-set diploids.
  Within-set Co diploids are not outgroups to Cbp-Co (003: Cbp-Co is ~5 SNP/kb from them,
  they are 0.9 apart).
- New alignments (asm10, run with 002's `002_align_syri.sh` via `LIST`/`OUTROOT`/`PRESET`
  overrides), all in `results/00_cross_syri/`:
  - 9 Co diploid x Cr/Cg diploid pairs (`data/pairs_cross.tsv`; summary in `results/00_cross_summary/`)
  - 18 Cbp subgenome x opposite-set diploid pairs (`data/pairs_cbp_cross.tsv`)
  - preset pilot (Co39 vs Cr145, `results/pilot_asm10|asm20`): asm10 gave 105 vs 92 Mb
    syntenic and 24 vs 38 Mb unaligned, so asm10 for all.

## Method (`scripts/001_polarize.py`)
Each event is expressed in the coordinates of a frame genome X (A or B of the pair) and
tested against X-vs-outgroup alignments:
- carrier = X: outgroup lacks it if >=70% of the interval lies in an X-only indel of the
  X-vs-O alignment -> insertion on X; outgroup has it if >=70% is in aligned blocks
  (SYNAL/INVAL/TRANSAL/INVTRAL/DUPAL/INVDPAL) -> deletion on the other genome.
- carrier = other genome: outgroup has an insertion of similar size (x0.5-2) within 50 bp
  -> deletion on X; flanks aligned with no indel -> insertion on the other genome.
- INV/TRANS/INVTR: O syntenic over the interval -> change on the other genome; O has the same
  SV type -> change on X.
- Per frame, the consensus is the unique plurality over 3 outgroups; the two frames are
  then reconciled: `both` agree, `A_frame_only`/`B_frame_only`, `conflict`, or `none`.
- HDR blocks are NOT counted as "outgroup has it" (they are diverged and TE-rich; counting
  them made F-carried events look like deletions on the other genome).
- Why two frames: with a single frame, F-lineage changes need an explicit breakpoint in
  the F-vs-O alignment while G-lineage changes are the default, giving a ~4:1 skew toward G
  even for symmetric diploid pairs. Two-frame reconciliation removes it (diploid-diploid
  ins/del now ~1:1 between lineages).

Outputs (`results/`, gitignored): `01_polarized/<pair>.tsv` (per event, per-outgroup calls
for both frames, final call + confidence) and `polarization_summary.tsv`.

    cd analyses/004_sv_polarization
    python3 scripts/001_polarize.py ../002_alignment/data/pairs.tsv \
        ../002_alignment/results/02_syri results/00_cross_syri results

## First look (preliminary)
Indels >= 50 bp, final calls with a decided lineage, diploid x Cbp pairs, summed over
pairs (not independent):

| lineage | deletions | insertions | ins:del |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cbp-Co | 4787 | 4341 | 0.91 |
| Co diploids | 4258 | 7451 | 1.75 |
| Cbp-Cr | 4360 | 3460 | 0.79 |
| Cr/Cg diploids | 5899 | 6802 | 1.15 |

Cbp subgenomes are deletion-biased relative to the diploids. Not yet tested for
significance or controlled for assembly differences.

## Caveats
- 38k of 81k diploid x Cbp indel events and ~11k of 18k diploid-diploid events stay
  ambiguous (`none`); about 32% of all diploid x Cbp events (~62% of decided calls) are
  single-frame. Filter on `confidence`.
- 'Conflict' calls (~5%) are excluded from the table.
- Diploid lineage totals include the larger CoMosher/CgMosher assemblies (extra TE
  insertions); pairs share genomes so counts are not independent.
- Cross-species Co x Cr/Cg pairs are not themselves polarized (no outgroup); only
  summarized in `results/00_cross_summary/`.
- Structural variant calls (INV/TRANS/INVTR) are mostly ambiguous and not reviewed here.

## Plots
    Rscript scripts/002_plots.R     # -> results/02_plots/*.png|pdf
`indel_by_lineage` (del vs ins per lineage, both-frame vs single-frame),
`indel_ratio_per_pair` (ins:del per pair; Mosher pairs marked; the Cbp-Co lineage is
bimodal across pairs, ~0.35 vs ~1.5), `outcome_mix` (both / single-frame / ambiguous /
conflict by pair class). Descriptive only.
